\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Closes At Record Low 11.222/Dlr; Euro Cited \b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 21:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY -(Dow Jones)- Mexico's peso slid to a new closing low against the dollar Wednesday as the euro made further gains against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid heightened war concerns. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City on 48-hour spot dollar markets, Banamex quoted the peso closing at a midrate of 11.2220 to the dollar, weaker than its opening of MXN11.1780 and Tuesday's MXN11.13 close. \par \par \uc2  Spreads at the close were MXN11.2120/11.2320 compared with 11.12/11.14 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A Mexico City trader said the peso had support at MXN11.25, with offers as high as MXN11.23 and settlements as high MXN22.70 during the session. \par \par \uc2  The trader said euro gains against the dollar were a key factor Wednesday. "Volume was quite brisk. It wasn't just people adjusting positions but some strong speculation," he added. \par \par \uc2  A possible range for Thursday is MXN11.17 to MXN11.25, the trader said. \par \par \uc2  In a report Wednesday, HSBC noted the almost total correlation between the peso/dollar and the dollar/euro in recent months, and hinted at expectations of action by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been considered, and then downplayed, but could yet be used as the peso sell-off continues." HSBC said. "More likely though, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will try once again to raise rates to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but as before, this will have a limited effect in the face of a weaker dollar." \par \par \uc2  Interest rates rose sharply Tuesday at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's primary auction, as investors demanded higher returns on debt in a weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The yield on benchmark 28-day Treasury bills was 9.6%, up from 9.3% the week before. \par \par \uc2  New York-based IDEAglobal said it expects the peso to trade between MXN11.10 and MXN11.30 in the coming weeks. \par \par \uc2  IDEAglobal also noted expectations that foreign direct investment this year will fall from 2002 levels, covering only three-quarters of the projected current account deficit, compared with nearly all of last year's deficit. \par \par \uc2  -By Anthony Harrup, Dow Jones Newswires; (5255) 5080-3450, anthony.harrup@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1027 1852 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030305dz3500182\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
