\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Opens At 10.8790/Dlr Vs 10.8750 Fri Close \b0\par\par\uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2003\par 16:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY -(Dow Jones)- Mexico's peso opened little changed against the dollar Monday as market participants awaited the U.N. weapons inspectors' report on Iraq, scheduled for delivery to the U.N. Security Council on Monday morning. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City around 1535 GMT, on 48-hour spot dollar markets, Banamex quoted the peso trading at a midrate of MXN10.8730, stronger from its opening level of MXN10.8790 and from Friday's MXN10.8750 close. \par \par \uc2  Banamex quoted a spread of MXN10.8630/10.8830, compared with MXN10.86/10.89 at Friday's close, which was an all-time  closing low the for peso. \par \par \uc2  Worries about a U.S. attack on Iraq have been at the heart of the recent pressure on the peso, which has been weakening as the dollar loses ground against the euro. \par \par \uc2  "The Mexican peso remains prisoner to the dollar," FXbriefing said in a report Monday. \par \par \uc2  The peso weakened sharply Friday after the Bank of Mexico left its monetary policy unchanged - against the expectations of most participants, who anticipated a tightening. \par \par \uc2  In its policy report, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it expects the current volatility - which includes a dose of speculation - to be temporary. \par \par \uc2  The report followed comments by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Guillermo Ortiz, who said the bank wasn't ruling out any options for countering volatility and speculation. \par \par \uc2  A number of analysts and traders said they expect the market to test the bank's resolve to back the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it  aims to bring inflation down to 3% this year. \par \par \uc2  The last time the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the exchange market was September 1998, during the Russian crisis. \par \par \uc2  President Vicente Fox, speaking in Davos on Saturday, reiterated his government's commitment to a free-floating exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  All Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have suffered similarly in  recent days. Over the past two years, Mexico's peso has fared better than other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Fox said. \par \par \uc2  "Our peso has handled this turbulence well and is in good conditions," Fox added. "Precisely because of that, we will continue the floating system, and we are not going to alter it." \par \par \uc2  -By Anthony Harrup, Dow Jones Newswires; (5255) 5080-3450, anthony.harrup@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1027 1852 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030127dz1r000xs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
