\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Closes Weaker At MXN9.8500/Dollar \b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 August 2002\par 21:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY -(Dow Jones)- Mexico's peso weakened against the dollar Thursday, affected partly by pressure on Brazil's real and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the South American country. \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  City on 48-hour spot dollar markets, Banamex  quoted the peso closing at a midrate of MXN9.8500 per dollar on a spread of MXN9.84/9.86. \par \par \uc2  That was weaker from its opening level of MXN9.8450 per dollar and from Wednesday's MXN9.8050 close. \par \par \uc2  Analysts expressed some surprise at the weakening, since U.S. stocks were moving higher and the dollar gained  against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - both usually positive factors for the peso. \par \par \uc2  In Brazil, however, there was renewed pressure on the real that led the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars. \par \par \uc2  "I think that had an effect on the market," said Antonio Magana, head \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at the Interacciones brokerage. \par \par \uc2  The peso also weakened Wednesday despite the announcement by HSBC of the U.K. that it will pay $1.14 billion for Mexico's Bital bank. Acquisitions imply foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows and tend to strengthen the peso. \par \par \uc2  Market participants were looking ahead to the release at 1930 GMT of inflation data for the first half of August. Market expectations are for a 0.15% increase in the Consumer Price Index. \par \par \uc2  "I expect the number will be in line, but a worse number could affect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Magana said. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the Finance Ministry will report the trade balance for July. \par \par \uc2  -By Anthony Harrup, Dow Jones Newswires; (52) 55-5080-3450; anthony.harrup@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1027 1852 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020823dy8m000oi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
