\par\par \b \uc2  Mexican peso falls after  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 189 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2000\par 19:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY, June 26 (Reuters) - The Mexican peso tumbled in late trading on Monday despite an afternoon \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buoy the sliding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of Sunday's presidential election. \par \par \uc2  The peso has weakened steadily since late last week, fluctuating on shaky volume ahead of the July 2 vote and the U.S. Federal Reserve meeting on interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark 48-hour peso lost 10.5 centavos to 10.0300/10.0500 to the dollar while the 24-hour contract weakened 10.3 centavos to 10.0250/10.0450. \par \par \uc2  Just after midday in Mexico City, Banco de Mexico tightened its monetary policy, raising the amount of liquidity it withholds from the local money market each day to 230 million pesos from a prior 200 million pesos. The mechanism, known as leaving the money market "short," is aimed at raising local interest rates to bolster the peso. \par \par \uc2  Before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move, the 48-hour peso contract was 8.9 centavos weaker in trading against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  ((-Kristin Roberts, Mexico City newsroom, +525 728 9549)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw6q02xwc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
