\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-Mexican peso drops on election jitters. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Julia Denegre \par \uc2 438 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2000\par 21:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY, June 6 (Reuters) - The Mexican peso fell by 1.89 percent on Tuesday amid increasing uncertainty over the outcome of the July 2 presidential and congressional elections, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark 48-hour peso contract closed 18.5 centavos weaker at 9.67/9.68 to the dollar, down 1.89 percent against the Monday close, as market players took up positions in greenbacks ahead of the polls. \par \par \uc2  The market was less concerned about who wins the election than how the results of the hotly contested election is taken by the loser, analysts and traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The market has incentives to hold (long dollar positions), above all before the elections," one trader said. "The electoral problem is not who wins, but how the losing candidate reacts." \par \par \uc2  The Institutional Revolutionary Party (PRI) is facing its stiffest challenge in its 71-year hold on the Mexican presidency, with its candidate Francisco Labastida in a tight race with Vicente Fox of the conservative National Action Party (PAN). \par \par \uc2  Labastida, holding a slim lead over Fox in the latest opinion polls, said on Monday Mexico could face social unrest if the PRI wins the elections by a small margin. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the sliding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said analyst Eligio San Juan at BBV-Probursa. \par \par \uc2  "The exchange rate can move other variables," said San Juan. "If it depreciates too much, the authorities will have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could increase the 'short'," he added. \par \par \uc2  The "short" is an instrument the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses to regulate market liquidity. It has been tightened twice so far this year. \par \par \uc2  "The proximity of the election is complicating the peso market, owing to the possibility of a very close result," said Cesar Castro, director of analysis at the Centre of Analysis and Economic Forecasts for Mexico (CAPEM). \par \par \uc2  He said the election nerves would probably last until a month after the election. \par \par \uc2  The peso fall undermined Mexican stocks, with the leading IPC index dropping about 273 points, or 4.2 percent. \par \par \uc2       Other helpful Mexican market information: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    * Main percentage gainers\tab \tab \par    * Main percentage decliners\tab \tab \par    * Most traded shares\tab \tab \tab \par    * Market statistics\tab \tab \tab \par    * Mexican ADRs\tab \tab \tab \tab \par    * Mexican ADRs/Bolsa equivalent\tab \tab \par    * Mexican futures (MexDer)\tab \tab \tab \par    * Mexican peso\tab \tab \tab \tab \par    * Mexican peso bids\tab \tab \tab \par    * Mexican Cetes rates\tab \tab \tab \par    * Mexican indicators forecast\tab \par    * Indices display\tab \tab \tab \tab \par    * Sector display\tab \tab \tab \tab \par    * Warrants\tab \tab \tab \tab \tab \par    * Buyer/Seller IDs\tab \tab \tab \par    * Brokerage characters\tab \tab \tab \par    * Detailed information\tab \tab \tab \par    * Mexican market overview\tab \tab \par    * Mexican oil prices\tab \tab \tab \par    * Domestic guide\tab \tab \tab \tab \par    * Country news\tab \tab \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Other Latin American markets:\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    * Argentina's MerVal\tab \tab \tab \par    * Brazil's Bovespa\tab \tab \tab \par    * Chile's IPSA\tab \tab \tab \tab \par    * Peru's IGRA\tab \tab \tab \tab \par    * Venezuela'