\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2  Peso Ends -2: Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 253 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 1999\par 21:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso closed sharply weaker Tuesday despite the Bank of Mexico's attempts to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as investors bailed out of Latin American markets on reports of a brewing political scandal in Brazil. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City on 48-hour spot dollar markets, banking leader Banamex quoted the peso closing at a midrate of 9.6200 per dollar (MXN), weaker from its open of MXN9.5400 and sharply weaker from its close of MXN9.4100 Friday. \par \par \uc2  Spreads at the close were MXN9.6100/9.6300 compared with 9.4050/9.4150 at the close Monday. Other banks quoted closing spreads ranging from MXN9.6100/9.6200 to MXN9.6250/9.6350. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by offering $200 million in dollars on the open market through an automatic mechanism that is activated when the peso weakens by more than 2% in one session. It sold $65 million to commercial banks at an average rate of MXN9.5742. \par \par \uc2  The peso opened sharply weaker on news reports that Brazilian President Fernando Henrique Cardoso had favored certain companies in the sale of telecommunications holding Telebras. \par \par \uc2  "There was strong demand for dollars among foreigners who wanted to pull their money out of all of Latin America, not just Mexico," said one trader. \par \par \uc2  The amount the peso weakened "makes us think that the peso was oversold," said Manuel Abreau, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Inverlat. \par \par 