\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil monetary policy aims to control inflation. \b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 1999\par 18:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRASILIA, Jan 29 (Reuters) - Brazil's current monetary policy is designed to keep inflation in check following a sharp devaluation of the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Francisco Lopes said Friday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may set targets for inflation after the real lost more than 41 percent of its value against the dollar in barely two weeks, stoking fears of a return of hyper-inflation, Lopes told foreign correspondents in an interview. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  planned to start publishing the level of its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves daily from Feb. 1 to quash the perception that continued high daily dollar outflows are sapping its foreign cash reserves, he said. \par \par \uc2  "We are going to start publishing them from Monday, given this situation, this absurd thing of people reading the (dollar) flow statistics in completely the wrong way," Lopes said. \par \par \uc2  "Clearly, any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on our part will be known on the following day. For us to give the market security, it is good to give it transparency," he added. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves remained around $36 billion, which includes about $9 billion from an international rescue package sponsored by the International Monetary Fund (IMF), he said. \par \par \uc2  The country would have to adopt a logical model for \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the one used in \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 , where the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  automatically \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the peso fluctuates by more than a certain percentage level, said Lopes. \par \par \uc2  In a bid to increase the flow of dollars to local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, drained by weeks of massive dollar outflows, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may again raise the limit of dollars local banks are allowed to sell as it did earlier this week, he said. \par \par \uc2  Lopes also dismissed growing speculation that Brazil might default on its local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt due to the devaluation and high interest rates. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday raised the benchmark market rate to 37 percent from 35.5 percent in what economists said was a bid to control the real's slide. \par \par \uc2  "To think that we will have rollover problems demonstrates you don't understand anything about Brazil," he said. \par \par \uc2  ((-Brasilia newsroom 5561 314-1193, fax 5561 223-5918, raquel.stenzel@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1t05j2e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
