\par\par \b \uc2  Mexican Peso -2: Brazil's  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2 , Equity Markets Eyed \b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 1999\par 15:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (Dow Jones)--Mexico's peso was marginally stronger against the dollar in early trade Thursday as tranquility returned to Brazilian markets, loosening the pressure against the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City a little before 1400 GMT, on 48-hour spot dollar markets, banking leader Banamex quoted the peso trading at a mid rate of 10.4050 per dollar against 10.5050 per dollar at Wednesday's close. Spreads were 10.3800/10.4300 pesos per dollar, compared with 10.4800/10.5300 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "Wednesday was crazy, and today (Thursday) the market looks much calmer," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader from a local brokerage. "Investors are placing a few peso purchase orders and we expect spreads to narrow throughout the session. Everyone is keeping an eye on Brazil." \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, Mexico Stock Exchange's key IPC index plunged 4.6% and the peso closed sharply weaker on concerns related to the resignation of Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president and the subsequent de facto devaluation of the real. \par \par \uc2  As reported, Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  discarded its mini trading band and adjusted its wide band to BRR1.20-1.32 per dollar from BRR1.12-1.22 per dollar. Wednesday's policy change caused an effective devaluation of the real of about 8.2%. \par \par \uc2  The move pressured regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly the free-floating Mexican peso, which depreciated by 3.5% at Wednesday's close and weakened as far as MXN11.2000 per dollar in intraday trading. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by selling $200 million Wednesday, in an auction that occurs when the peso-dollar spot rate is 2% above a fixed level set the previous day by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  based on a sample of spot rates. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 14-01-99 \par \par \uc2  1425GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 1852 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1e00bmg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
