\par\par \b \uc2  Fresh dollar auction unlikely - Banco de Mexico. \b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1999\par 19:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY, Jan 13 (Reuters) - Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would continue operating within the terms of its scheme of contingent dollar sales to support the peso and was not considering fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to alter the terms of its contingency scheme in order to carry out a fresh dollar sale, but a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  source said that was not currently on the cards. \par \par \uc2  "I insist, today that is not the theme," he told Reuters. "I don't want to say it is ruled out or not ruled out,...but the bank is continuing to operate under the established scheme." \par \par \uc2  Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday, auctioning $200 million at an average exchange rate of 10.6321 pesos per dollar. \par \par \uc2  That took place under the terms of an automatic mechanism set up to support Mexico's floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should it shed more than 2.0 percent of its value against the previous day's official fixing rate. \par \par \uc2  The scheme allows the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell a maximum of $200 million per day over three auction opportunities. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold its full $200 million quota at 9:15 a.m. (1515 GMT), when the benchmark 48-hour peso was trading at 10.75 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Tuesday's fix, or reference rate, was 10.048 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  After the auction the peso weakened further, to 10.76/0.80 to the dollar, though it later moderated some of its decline. At 12:06 p.m. (1806 GMT) the 48-hour peso was trading at 10.50/10.53 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The source said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained vigilant over the market's moves. \par \par \uc2  "The market has brought the peso rate against the dollar down a bit, so in some way yes (we are satisfied with the auction), but we remain very attentive to the fact that the time of greatest demand is between 12:00 a.m and 1:00 p.m. (1800 and 1900 GMT)." \par \par \uc2  Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market closes at 1.30 p.m. \par \par \uc2  The source said it was unlikely that a second auction would take place before the close. \par \par \uc2  "All that's being said here is that in the coming days (such) \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be carried out," he added. ((Caroline Brothers, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 7905; mexicocity.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1d06n2v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
