\par\par \b \uc2  Mexican  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  wages war on speculators. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Andrew Hurst \par \uc2 656 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 1998\par 00:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY, Sept 11 (Reuters) - The guardians of Mexico's battered peso have a fight to the finish on their hands as they seek to bolster the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to become a victim of the world's emerging market woes. \par \par \uc2  Because Mexico has one of the most liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets of any emerging market country, the peso has become a soft target for speculators seeking to place proxy bets against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - such as Brazil's real - which they believe are heading for a fall. \par \par \uc2  "It's the biggest most liquid emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," said a New York banker who asked not to be named. \par \par \uc2  "If you want to bet on Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakening you simply short the (Mexican) peso," he added. \par \par \uc2  The peso closed at an all-time low for the third day running on Friday with the benchmark 48-hour peso shedding seven centavos to end at 10.58/10.62 against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  But for Mexico's monetary authorities there is more at stake than national self-respect. As the peso has plunged, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has hiked interest rates, fuelling fears that the economy will be tipped into recession. \par \par \uc2  "The peso has become one of the thermometers of emerging market sentiment," said Juan Pablo Chavez at IDEA in New York. \par \par \uc2  Some funds have been using the peso as a hedging device against other emerging market instruments. \par \par \uc2  "You buy-high yield Thai bonds or Ukrainian treasury bills and then hedge it by shorting the peso," an economist with a large investment bank in New York. \par \par \uc2  The peso's role as a punching bag for nervous investors in emerging markets has driven down the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value to a point that it is widely seen as undervalued in relation to the real state of health of the Mexican economy. \par \par \uc2  "The peso has reached levels that have stopped reflecting economic fundamentals" said Chavez. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Mexico, ever sensitive to the threat to inflation posed by a fallen peso, has tightened liquidity and hiked interest rates in recent weaks in an effort to brake the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall but to no avail. \par \par \uc2  But now the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to be ready to take off the gloves and to mix it up with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Guillermo Ortiz declared on Thursday he was prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market whenever he saw fit. The Bank of Mexico did as much earlier in the day with a discretionary sale of $278 million outside a pre-settled automatic \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  mechanism in which it sold an additional $200 million. \par \par \uc2  The prospect of random \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the peso appears to have put the hedgers on the defensive. "The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market may cease to be an efficient hedge against emerging market risk, said Chavez. \par \par \uc2  One trader said on Friday: "right now nobody wants to buy excessive (dollar) positions because it could turn out to be very expensive if Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  "This latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has altered the rules of the game and ... this should increase the cost of this hedge," he said. \par \par \uc2  One of the most alarming aspects of the slide in the peso, which has lost 23 percent of its value against the dollar this year, has been its tendency to feed on itself as Mexican investors take fright and dump the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Mexico's long history of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  instability has instilled strong survival instincts among Mexicans who tend to take to their heels as soon as they sense that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is coming under strong pressure. \par \par \uc2  "You also have an overreaction in Mexico because those people who did not switch into dollars in time in the past got burned," said Jonathan Heath, an independent economist based in Mexico City. \par \par \uc2  "You can't blame them, it's perfectly rational behaviour," he added. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9b00wit\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
