\par\par \b \uc2  Banco de Mexico says sold $278 mln to support peso. \b0\par\par\uc2 460 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1998\par 23:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY, Sept 10 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the "discretional \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " it undertook earlier on Thursday to support the peso totalled $278 million pesos. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market suffered unusual pressure today derived from a deterioriation in the international financial situation," Banco de Mexico said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  "Given this situation the (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's) Exchange Commission, made up of members if the Finance Ministry and the Banco de Mexico, instructed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to directly sell $278 million in the market in order to give it liquidity and reduce its volatility," it said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in the form of a dollar sale, came in addition to an automatic $100 million auction that was triggered earlier in the session when the peso lost 2.0 percent of its value against the greenback. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  undertook the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shed 40 centavos to a record low of 10.73 pesos per dollar after the automatic auction took place. \par \par \uc2  The extra dollar sale pushed the peso back up to 10.35 per dollar, leaving it two centavos weaker than Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  It ended Thursday at 10.55 pesos to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  During the morning the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctioned $100 million at an average price of 10.577 pesos per dollar. \par \par \uc2  A second dollar auction, scheduled for 11 a.m. local (1600 GMT), did not take place because the peso had not fallen another two percent after the earlier auction. \par \par \uc2  Separately, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to tighten monetary policy a fifth time this year, increasing the amount by which it keeps the money market short each day to 100 million pesos from 70 million pesos \par \par \uc2  In a separate statement Banco de Mexico said this was designed to contain \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility. \par \par \uc2  "The Governing board repeats its conviction that the referred to volatility is out of line with the basic conditions of the Mexican economy," it said. \par \par \uc2  "In order to counteract this volatility and bring order to the country's financial markets, to preserve sustained economic development and inflation objectives congruent with this objective, the governing board of Banco de Mexico has decided to restrict monetary policy further. \par \par \uc2  "Banco de Mexico is aware of the impact the increase in the cost of credit has on various key parts of the economy, but it feels that this is a necessary stabilising factor given current circumstances," it said. \par \par \uc2  Turbulence emanating from Russia and Asia has hit all emerging markets including Mexico, which has been trying to minimise the impact on its economy as its floating peso bears the brunt of the storms. \par \par \uc2  ((Caroline Brothers, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 7905; mexicocity.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9a00uuf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
