\par\par \b \uc2  Banco de Mexico sells $100 mln to halt peso slide. \b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1998\par 17:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY, Sept 10 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to shore up the battered peso, selling $100 million at an average of 10.5577 pesos per dollar, Banco de Mexico said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The move came as the benchmark 48-hour peso\tab \tab     lost 26.5 centavos to 10.58/10.595 per dollar in the first hour of trade.\par Meanwhile, the rate on overnight Cetes soared 650 basis points on the secondary money market\tab    to 40 percent and Mexican stocks were off more than five percent, flirting with the psychological 3,000-point barrier on the IPC index\tab  .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has an automatic mechanism to inject dollars into the banking system when the peso loses more than two percent of its value within a trading day. \par \par \uc2  Banco de Mexico said it offered $200 million at auction between 9 a.m. and 9:15 a.m. (1400 and 1415 GMT) but received only $100 million in bids. The remaining $100 million would be offered from 11 a.m. to 11:15 a.m. (1600 to 1615 GMT), it said. \par \par \uc2  Bids ranged from 10.5569 to 10.5601 per dollar. Dollars were assigned to six bidders who made 10 bids, Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  Automatic \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were first introduced in February 1997, and recently were triggered on Aug. 21 and Aug. 26. \par \par \uc2  Following the Aug. 26 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  changed its rules on the mechanism, allowing up to three auctions per day to sell a total $200 million. Previously, there was only one auction for up to $200 million. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mexican financial markets were rocked on Thursday by continued turmoil in Brazil\tab   , which has become a recent bellwether for Latin America, and the Dow\tab  , which fell on concern over U.S. President Bill Clinton's political woes.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7902)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9a00to0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
