\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico peso closes at record low on Brazil,Clinton. \b0\par\par\uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1998\par 21:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MEXICO CITY, Sept 10 (Reuters) - The Mexican peso\tab \tab     closed at a historic low versus the dollar on Thursday after a tumultuous day in which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  took three separate steps to shore up the ailing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The benchmark 48-hour peso ended 22 centavos weaker at 10.52/10.55 per dollar after financial haemorrhaging in Brazil soured investors on the rest of Latin America and U.S. President Bill Clinton's political woes spread to Wall Street stocks, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  The 48-hour peso has lost 23.55 percent of its value versus the dollar this year. It had been even lower at one point in the morning, setting a new intraday low when it had shed 40 centavos to 10.73 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The 24-hour peso fell even further at the close, losing 33 centavos to end at 10.55/10.65 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice offered dollar sales in order to prevent the slide and then tightened monetary policy in a bid to increase interest rates and thus protect the peso. \par \par \uc2  "Brazil is exerting a lot of pressing on the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of a possible devaluation and the falling share prices there," one \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Brazil's Bovespa index\tab    was off 12.5 percent in late trade amid a massive capital outflow from the country.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Clinton's problems are hitting the peso hard," another trader said as pressure mounted in Washington to begin impeachment hearings because of the Monica Lewinsky scandal.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par When the peso lost two percent of its value versus the dollar in early trade, that triggered an automatic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  auction of dollars, and $100 million was injected into the banking system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Banco de \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Mexico\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  later exercised a "discretional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 " by adding an undisclosed amount of dollars to the system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Then it announced it was tightening monetary policy for the fifth time this year by reducing liquidity in the secondary money market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  now will leave the market "short" each day by 100 million pesos instead of the previous 70 million.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Gina Moreno, Mexico City newsroom, +525 728-9555)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9a00t57\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
