\par\par \b \uc2  Mexican peso keeps sliding despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 229 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1998\par 17:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY, Sept 10 (Reuters) - The Mexican peso continued to slide versus the dollar on Thursday despite an automatic \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  designed to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it loses more than two percent of its value in a single trading day. \par \par \uc2  Battered by continued global market turmoil and a slump on Wall Street, the benchmark 48-hour peso shed 33 centavos to 10.64/10.66 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The contract had weakened as far as 10.73 per dollar, a historic intraday low, before moderating losses. \par \par \uc2  "The peso is being affected by the fall of share prices in New York, Mexico and Brazil," one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "The market is under a lot of pressure from negative speculation, and that is causing capital flight," added another trader. \par \par \uc2  Earlier on Thursday, the peso was so battered that it triggered an automatic \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction of dollars. Banco de Mexico said it sold $100 million in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from 9 a.m. to 9:15 a.m. (1400 to 1415 GMT). \par \par \uc2  Another $100 million could be auctioned from 11 a.m. to 11:15 (1600 to 1615 GMT), the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  The 24-hour peso was losing 32 centavos to 10.63/10.64 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  ((Gina Moreno, Mexico City newsroom, +525 728-9555)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021108du9a00sgi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\