\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Gurria, Ortiz To Hold News Conference At 2300 GMT \b0\par\par\uc2 140 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1998\par 22:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (Dow Jones)--Mexican Finance Minister Jose Angel Gurria and Bank of Mexico Governor Guillermo Ortiz will hold a joint news conference at 2300 GMT, the Finance Ministry said. \par \par \uc2  The ministry gave no details about what would be discussed. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since December 1995, outside of $200 million dollar auctions it holds whenever the peso (MXN) weakens 2.0% against the dollar from the previous day's fix. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it sold $278 million Thursday in addition to the $200 million auction. Despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the peso closed at a mid rate of MXN10.6000 to the dollar, sharply weaker than MXN10.3200 at Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 10-09-98 \par \par \uc2  2049GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du9a07te7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
