\par\par \b \uc2  Mexican overnight Cetes close lower on firm peso. \b0\par\par\uc2 169 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY, April 17 (Reuters) - Mexican overnight Cetes rates closed 40 basis points lower at 19.30 percent on Friday, driven down by foreign investors who were attracted by the strength of the peso, dealers and analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark 48-hour peso closed 0.9 centavos stronger at 8.4830/8.4850 to the dollar, riding a buying spree on the stock exchange to ward off speculation about a change in monetary policy and other factors that could weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There was a little more action from foreigners, which was directly reflected in the appreciation of the peso and the bolsa and some of those resources were directed toward the money market," one analyst said. \par \par \uc2  Rates, which move in the opposite direction to price, also came down when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  injected 356 million pesos of liquidity during its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  ((Fatima Escobar, \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  City newsroom, +525 728-7916, mexicocity.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du4h0786d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
