\par\par \b \uc2  Ortiz unlikely to change exchange policy - analysts. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Robert Kozak \par \uc2 535 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY, Dec 15 (Reuters) - Finance Minister Guillermo Ortiz, newly appointed as head of the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is unlikely to make in any radical changes in monetary policy, particularly to the exchange rate, economists said Monday. \par \par \uc2  President Ernesto Zedillo named Ortiz to become the new governor at Banco de Mexico on January 1, replacing retiring longtime \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Miguel Mancera, who oversaw a policy of a freely floating peso. \par \par \uc2  In his announcement late Sunday, Zedillo said he would propose that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  gain more say in setting exchange rate policy. \par \par \uc2  The finance minister now casts the deciding vote on the Exchange Commission, the joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  finance ministery body that sets exchange rate policy. It was not clear if this structure would change. \par \par \uc2  Some financial analysts speculated that Ortiz might move his country away from the free float the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  went to in late 1994. \par \par \uc2  Since the peso crash of December 1994, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has freely floated, with the Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  occasionally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  up until late 1996 to curb wild swings in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The economic think tank I.D.E.A. said in a market commentary that concern over Ortiz may increase in times of market crisis. \par \par \uc2  "The concern stems from the potential contradiction between the need for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain its perception of independence and Ortiz's recent history as a proponent of a weaker peso and higher growth," I.D.E.A said. \par \par \uc2  Many major Mexican exporters have complained that the peso is overvalued, eroding their foreign sales. However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been loath to weaken the peso versus the dollar, fearing that it could fuel inflation. \par \par \uc2  Even so, all economic analysts consulted by Reuters were confident the the current \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate policy is likely to remain in place. \par \par \uc2  Most economists played down the possibility of Mexico moving to a fixed rate system, perhaps based on the Chilean real trade weighted exchange rate band. \par \par \uc2  "Some people have said that Ortiz would want a system of bands for the exchange rate. Maybe he had that idea three or four yers ago, but I don't think he will keep to that idea given what has happened to that type of exchange rate regimes, particularly in Asia," said ING Barings economist Sergio Martin. \par \par \uc2  "If he had that idea, he has abandoned it. Besides we (Mexico) don't have enough reserves for it," Martin added. \par \par \uc2  "If this move was meant to make Banco de Mexico more independent, which I think it is, then a exchange rate band or any type of fixed exchange rate would subvert that. The minute the Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange rate they lose power, so I would suspect they will keep the current policy," Paribas economist John Welch said. \par \par \uc2  "Some of the talk that we are hearing is that Ortiz might be more inclined to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the peso. In fact our view, and I think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's view, is that the peso doesn't need to be weakened," said Lawrence Krohn, head of Latin American economic and equity research for UBS Securities. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtcf01192\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
