\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico peso ends firm as brokers enter money mkt. \b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY, April 17 (Reuter) - The Mexican peso extended early firmness at the close of trade on Thursday due to local and foreign brokers switching from dollars to invest in the domestic money market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "It is better for brokers to sell their dollars to have pesos to invest at very high rates in the money market," a trader said. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark 48-hour peso and its 24-hour stablemate ended 1.05 and two centavos firmer, respectively, at 7.8750/7.8775 and 7.8625/7.8650 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "As interest rates are so attractive, it is better to go short on dollars, and as that means the peso firms up, you win both ways," the trader said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said reduced pressure from the U.S. bond market had also shored up the peso.  The U.S. 30-year Treasury bond was down 10/32 to yield 7.07 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was closing in Mexico.  "Dealers are seeing that the time is ripe for switching to pesos.  The outlook is still for U.S. rates to go up, but not in the short term," another trader said, referring to the May 20 Federal Open Market Commitee meeting to review U.S. interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Same-day peso contracts had earlier closed two centavos firmer at 7.8660/7.8700 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers estimated the peso could remain at current levels until domestic interest rates begin to decline. \par \par \uc2  "Some banks are very short on dollars and will stay that way until Banco de Mexico lowers interest rates," a trader said.  "But we need to look out for how the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the secondary money market." \par \par \uc2  (( --Alexis Quiones, \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  City newsroom +525 728-9555)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4h06yvv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
