\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico peso ends stronger on certification hopes. \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY, Feb 28 (Reuter) - The Mexican peso clawed back some lost ground at the close on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the peso recovered as banks that had gone long on dollars stepped in to sell them ahead of expected recertification by the U.S. government of Mexico as an ally in the the war on drugs. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark 48-hour peso and its 24-hour stablemate ended 3.4 and 2.5 centavos firmer, respectively, at 7.9400/7.9460 and 7.9350/7.9450 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The peso recovered as the market has already discounted Mexico's certification," a trader said. \par \par \uc2  News that U.S. Secretary of State Albright recommended recertification for Mexico came just five minutes after the close of trade in Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Traders noted Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market as speculation had eased considerably since Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected to accept bids from banks to buy dollars if the peso reached a rate of 7.9925 per dollar by 1200 local time/1800 GMT, or two percent weaker than the official fixing rate published in Friday's edition of the Mexican Government Official Gazette. \par \par \uc2  This rate was surpassed in early trade, but the peso began to firm up mid-morning so the criteria for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  never crystallized. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they expected more banks to sell more long dollar positions on Monday after certification was confirmed. \par \par \uc2  "Yesterday's (peso) onslaught was out of order. Dealers overbought dollars and they dumped part of their positions today," another dealer said. "So now we have certification, they will certainly offload the rest on Monday." \par \par \uc2  Same-day peso contracts had earlier closed 14 centavos weaker at 7.9550/7.9650 per dollar, after lagging the market. \par \par \uc2  ((-- Alexis Quiones, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9555)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt2s09f32\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
