\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Of Mexico/Auctions-3:Could Thwart Speculative Attacks \b0\par\par\uc2 277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 1997\par 15:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  If the dollar-buying mechanism doesn't prompt the peso to depreciate gradually in line with inflation, many analysts say sharper adjustment pressures could resurface by April. And that's when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's program to sell dollars to stem big exchange rate swings could become a useful tool - especially if the swings take place amid thin, speculative trading as they did during late 1995. \par \par \uc2  'It could cut down on speculative attacks,' said Hector Chavez, economist with Santander Investment in Mexico City. 'In 1995 and even in 1996 there was a game with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to see when and where they would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This is different, because they're not signalling an exchange rate target.' \par \par \uc2  At least one observer, though, questions why the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not opt for the more traditional tool of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  'Oftentimes limited \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be more effective,' said Lawrence Goodman, economist with Salomon Brothers in New York. 'It could dampen those pressures without disclosure of dollar sales.' \par \par \uc2  But others argue that Mexico's newly independent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  really has no choice, because it's still busy trying to build a solid track record in the wake of the December 1994 peso devaluation and ensuing turmoil. \par \par \uc2  'Group of Seven countries don't have credibility problems, but the Bank of Mexico has to be as transparent as possible,' said Jonathan Heath, a \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  City-based economist. He added that the undisclosed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  practices of other central banks 'would be a disaster' for Mexico at this time. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-02-97 \par \par \uc2  1412GMT \par \par \uc2  1191 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2l01ep7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
