\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS - Mexico's Mancera defends peso policy. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Henry Tricks \par \uc2 488 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY, Nov 14 (Reuter) - Banco de Mexico Governor Miguel Mancera on Thursday defended his policy of maintaining a free-floating peso, arguing that a permanently undervalued exchange rate may do as much harm as good. \par \par \uc2  At the end of a year of relative exchange-rate stability, in which he was criticised by some sectors when the peso's margin of undervaluation against the dollar shrank, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief stressed his prime duty was controlling inflation. \par \par \uc2  For instance, when the peso began a slide in October, Banco de Mexico left the money markets short of 20 million pesos to push up interest rates to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from fueling inflation. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Mexico made this decision because large and abrupt increases in the exchange rate bring about inflationary consequences that, in the end, make it more difficult to bring rates down," Mancera said. \par \par \uc2  In October, the peso slid from around 7.5 pesos per dollar to eight pesos. On Thursday, the benchmark 48-hour or spot contract closed at 7.9050/7.9080 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Giving his reasons for the steep October peso drop, Mancera said uncertainty ahead of the signing of an economic recovery pact, problems with petrochemical and rail privatizations, and accumulated inflation differentials between the United States and Mexico played their parts. \par \par \uc2  But wheras some sectors, such as exporters, had argued that a steep peso drop was long overdue, Mancera indicated that he did not favor maintaining a permanently undervalued exchange rate to foster economic growth. \par \par \uc2  "Even though there are some groups that apparently benefit from a permanently undervalued exchange rate, there are also those who would suffer from such a situation," he said. \par \par \uc2  "It should be recalled that an ever undervalued exchange rate perpetuates the depression of real wages and the existence of high inflation and interest rates. This effects consumption, investment and, consequently, economic performance as a whole." \par \par \uc2  "The idea that a permanently undervalued exchange rate fosters economic growth, or that it is beneficial to all, is not persuasive," he said. \par \par \uc2  On the other hand, he said Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year to stop gradual depreciations brought on by market forces. \par \par \uc2  "It must also be emphasized that the current monetary and exchange-rate policies are in no way designed to forestall the depreciation of the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , should the fundamental conditions of the economy so warrant," he said. \par \par \uc2  Referring to the performance of the economy, he reiterated that it was expected to achieve at least four percent growth this year and next, noting that as well as export growth, "in 1996 it is already possible to recognize the positive contributions of consumption and investment." \par \par \uc2  Export momentum continued strong, he said, and year-end inflation was expected to be around half last year's level of 52 percent. \par \par \uc2  -- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9560 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018dsbe00cys\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
