\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Opens -2: Range Of 7.7700-7.8000/Dlr Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 1996\par 16:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-Dow Jones)--Mexico's peso opened slightly stronger against the dollar in a quiet start to trading Thursday, with a slightly positive start to the day on the Mexican Stock Exchange helping calm recent peso volatility. \par \par \uc2  Traders expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trade in a range of 7.7700 per dollar to 7.8000 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City a little after 1400 GMT, on 48-hour spot dollar markets, banking leader Banamex quoted the peso opening at a mid rate of 7.7750 per dollar against 7.7850 per dollar at Wednesday's close. Spreads were 7.7700/7.7800 pesos per dollar, compared with 7.7800/7.7900 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Other banks had the spot dollar trading at a mid rate of 7.7900 pesos on a narrower spread of 7.7850/7.7950. \par \par \uc2  The peso's recent sharp weakenening movements - it weakened as far as 7.8600 per dollar in intraday trading Wednesday - were reversed in early afternoon trading Wednesday when trading banks decided to take profits. \par \par \uc2  Mexican financial authorities also tried to calm the markets by explaining their recent actions. Authorities said there had been no direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. But Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Miguel Mancera, in a rare release of testimony before legislators, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had decided to restrict liquidity to the banking system Monday to prevent a speculative spiral. \par \par \uc2  The slight drop in the yield on the U.S. 30-year Treasury bond is also helping keep the peso steady. The yield stands at around 6.83%, down from around 6.88% during Wednesday trading. \par \par \uc2  The Mexican Stock Exchange's key IPC index stands at 3272.15, up 9.14 points. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-10-96 \par \par \uc2  1419GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 1852 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dsah004fz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
