\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico News: Dornbusch Says Peso Not Free Floating \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 1996\par 16:37\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MONTERREY (Dow Jones)--The following news summary is based on Tuesday's editions of the Monterrey dailies El Norte, El Diario and El Financiero's Northeast Edition. \par \par \uc2  -- Rudiger Dornbusch, the influential and controversial economics professor from the Massachussetts Institute of Technology, accused the \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the peso strong against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "It's wrong to say that in Mexico there exists a free float of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , since the Bank of Mexico controls it so it won't move," El Norte reported Dornbusch as saying in a conference in the resort city of Cancun. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Mexico officials have repeatedly said this year they haven't interfered with the value of the peso. \par \par \uc2  Dornbusch said in his accusation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts to prop up the peso were "very irresponsible" and could damage Mexico's effort to grow its export industry. Exports, in four or five years, should account for 30% of economic production in order for Mexico to achieve 6% annual growth. \par \par \uc2  "... which will only happen with a competitive exchange rate," El Norte quoted Dornbusch as saying. \par \par \uc2  Mexico's peso closed at 7.53 pesos to the dollar on Monday, which is stronger than the year-end close of 7.69 pesos to the dollar, despite inflation so far in 1996 of 18.5%. \par \par \uc2  -- The debtors' rights group, El Barzon, demonstrated in several cities against the Mexican banking system and vowed to protect their properties from foreclosure on the day a government program to restructure debts and give interest rate reductions ended, Monterrey dailies reported. \par \par \uc2  Barzon members used different protest techniques to call attention to their cause, including riding elephants through Mexico City streets, smashing tomatoes in front of the Mexico's Banking Association building, painting signs in blood in Chihuahua and handing out packets of basic foodstuff in Nuevo Leon. \par \par \uc2  Barzon leaders said they would follow Monday's protest with more demonstrations against the banks. \par \par \uc2  -Thomas Black \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 01-10-96 \par \par \uc2  1437GMT \par \par \uc2  1802 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011013dsa100fky\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
