\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -2: No  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  In Peso Market \b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 1996\par 18:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it used the monetary base forecast in the government's economic program as the determining factor in keeping the money supply stable. It said that the 'evolution of the monetary base so far in 1996 has been in line with what was expected,' subject to a quarterly limit set on internal credit. \par \par \uc2  It said all of its goals: controlling inflation, market stability, economic growth, and structural reform, have seen 'significant advances.' \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said 'renewed confidence in the economic program, and in the economic prospects' of Mexico, have allowed interest rates to drop significantly. Bellwether rates on 28-day Treasury bills, or Cetes, have fallen from about 40% in January to about 24% now. \par \par \uc2  'That tendency to drop has been caused by market forces, and not artificially provoked by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's actions,' the Bank of Mexico said. \par \par \uc2  It also said it has allowed the peso to float freely and 'abstained from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, except in the monthly auctions in which it sells options to financial institutions to sell the Bank of Mexico a set limit of dollars. \par \par \uc2  'In general, the behavior of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in 1996 has resulted in an appreciation of the peso compared to the significant depreciation seen at the end of last year, which was a reflection of speculative pressures,' the bank said. \par \par \uc2  The peso closed 1995 at 7.6950 per dollar, weaker than the 7.5390 per dollar at which it closed Friday on 48-hour spot dollar markets. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 30-09-96 \par \par \uc2  1618GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds9u07uu2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
