\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Closes Weaker At 7.6050/Dollar \b0\par\par\uc2 288 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 1996\par 20:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-Dow Jones)--Mexico's peso closed weaker Thursday at higher U.S. interest rates attracted funds back north of the border. \par \par \uc2  In Mexico City on spot dollar markets, banking leader Banamex quoted the peso closing at a midrate of 7.6050 per dollar, stronger from its open of 7.6175 per dollar and weaker from its close Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Spreads at the close were 7.5950/7.6150 compared with 7.5800/7.6000 at the close Wednesday. Other banks quoted closing spreads of 7.6075/7.6125 and 7.6100/7.6150. \par \par \uc2  Traders said rates on 30-year U.S. Treasury bonds have reached 7.2%, pulling investors out of emerging markets 'to a more stable economy.' \par \par \uc2  Earlier in the day the peso had weakened to a midrate of 7.6415 per dollar, and several traders said they had expected it to remain at that level. \par \par \uc2  'I saw it staying weaker than 7.64,' said one trader. 'From what trading has been like all day and what the expectations are, it should be weaker,' \par \par \uc2  Another trader said the late afternoon strengthening of the peso occurred on a sudden supply of dollars, but noted the supply 'doesn't seem real.' \par \par \uc2  Some speculated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, a Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokeswoman denied any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and other traders said they had not seen any signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  activity. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets 25 times in 1995 to support the peso, according to its annual report released last week. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-06-96 \par \par \uc2  1851GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds6d04wv7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
