\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico/Peso -4: Peso Stable Despite Falling Interest Rates \b0\par\par\uc2 288 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 1996\par 14:00\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Many believe \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buying pesos, or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at key moments this year, to maintain the peso strong. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made several \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year. It later announced to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from going over 8 pesos to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  So far this year, it hasn't acknowledged any \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the peso. \par \par \uc2  If the government is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the peso, it should make its policy known and "not try to surprise traders" as it did last year, Fernandez said. \par \par \uc2  The only reason to suspect government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  lately on the peso is the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's surpising stability, despite pressure from falling interest rates, said Everardo Elizondo Almaguer, director of economic investigation for Bancomer SA. \par \par \uc2  "What we don't know is if (the government) has a specific policy on what is a high exchange rate and what is a low exchange rate," Elizondo said. \par \par \uc2  Interest rates on bellwether 28-day Treasury Certificates (CETES) have fallen to 25.58% at last Tuesday's auction from near 40% in mid-February. \par \par \uc2  Elizondo said most of the peso's resilience results from Mexico's speedy economic recovery that began to show signs at the first of the year. \par \par \uc2  "I see the Mexican economy pulling rapidly out of its crisis," he said. \par \par \uc2  Elizondo played down export-oriented companies' complaints that the stronger peso is making them less competitive on international markets. \par \par \uc2  "I see the external sector is very good condition," he said. "(Exporters) need to prove first that the exchange rate at the present level has really impacted their ability to export." \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES EMERGING MARKETS REPORT 06-04-96 \par \par \uc2  0800EDT \par \par \uc2  (Corrected 0935EDT) \par \par \uc2  1802 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020011013ds6400c7b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
