\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Opens -2: Awaiting Cetes Results Tuesday \b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par 16:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY (AP-Dow Jones)--Mexico's peso opened slightly stronger Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Banking leader Banamex quoted the peso on 48-hour spot markets opening at a midrate of 7.5975 pesos per dollar. The peso then strengthened slightly to 7.5925 per dollar around 1530 GMT, a touch stronger from 7.6000 per dollar at the close Monday. Spreads were 7.5825/7.6025 compared with 7.5900/7.6100 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  'The market is expecting a rise in interest rates to contain the dollar,' a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said. 'But they're not discounting that the peso should really be weaker.' \par \par \uc2  The peso is being supported by expectations that interest rates on benchmark 28-day Treasury bills, or Cetes, will rise between one and two percentage points from 42.27%. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to announce the results of its weekly auction after markets close Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Speculators are 'playing with' the exchange rate, the trader said, as they wait for the interest rate announcement. As well, many are also betting that the U.S. Federal Reserve will lower interest rates after its policy meeting later this week. \par \par \uc2  The trader said the peso should remain between 7.6000 and 7.6500 to the dollar, and expected the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it weakens more than that. \par \par \uc2  'These days it's under a lot of pressure,' he said. 'The dollar is very strong.' \par \par \uc2  But he said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to avoid using its slim international reserves to support the peso, and is likely to keep raising interest rates instead. \par \par \uc2  Spreads quoted by other banks put the peso at 7.5850/7.6050 and 7.5875/7.6075. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 12-03-96 \par \par \uc2  1530GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds3c026o4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
