\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso Opens -3: 7.6200/Dlr Seen Crucial Support \b0\par\par\uc2 245 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1996\par 17:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The peso weakened as poor economic prospects kept it under pressure, traders said. \par \par \uc2  At about 1600 GMT, banking leader Banamex quoted the 48-hour spot peso trading at 7.5925 per dollar, weaker from 7.5750 per dollar at the close Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The peso had opened at a mid-rate of 7.5900/dollar. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was under pressure despite the hike in bellwether interest rates. \par \par \uc2  'The rates were basically anticipated so the market saw no reason to react positively,' one trader noted. \par \par \uc2  If the peso continues to weaken, traders said it could force the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as it did several times last year when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped dramatically against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  'The Bank of Mexico could go in,' a trader said. 'The key is if the peso goes to 7.6200 (against the dollar), then it would be possible that the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 .' \par \par \uc2  He said he doubted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would make any move if the peso remained anywhere stronger that level. \par \par \uc2  Mexico's government has set a target year-average exchange rate of 7.70 pesos to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the peso was likely to remain around the 7.600 level during the day. While trading is stronger Wednesday than it has been all week, they said it still remains relatively weak. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 06-03-96 \par \par \uc2  1612GMT \par \pa