\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2 's Peso -2: Observers Cite  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Threat \b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Februar 1996\par 21:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The spot dollar mid rate soared as high as 7.6400 pesos in early trading before peso-selling pressures eased. Some traders attributed the peso recovery to a mild reversal in 30-year U.S. Treasury bonds and a corresponding stabilization in domestic secondary money market rates after a sharp rise early Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Market players were also cautious amid speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was poised to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the peso slid too quickly. \par \par \uc2  'I didn't see any direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but everyone was definitely aware of the possibility,' said one local dealer. \par \par \uc2  Some observers attributed the early peso sell-off to foreign institutions finalizing their positions ahead of the end of the month. Volume was heavy at the open, but fell off in later trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Traders added that a Standard & Poor's report issued Wednesday was drawing some attention. S&P affirmed its double-B ratings on Mexican long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  obligations and said the outlook remained negative. It said confidence remained 'fragile' and added that exchange rate volatility has 'seriously weakened the banking system, weighing on economic growth prospects.' \par \par \uc2  Adding to recent bearish market sentiment, Bear Stearns characterized Mexico's political situation as being 'in flux,' in a report late Wednesday, adding that it is underweight on the country. \par \par \uc2  The local stock market also continued to lose ground Thursday, with the key IPC index down 1.2% to 2,828.49 with less than an hour left in trading. The index fell 2.6% Wednesday to fall to a new 1996 closing low. Volume has slumped and prices have slipped in February after a spirited 9.2% run-up in the IPC in January. \par \par \uc2  The peso closed 0.5% weaker against the dollar from Thursday's close. The dollar ended January at 7.3650 pesos after closing out 1995 at 7.6950 pesos. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-02-96 \par \par \uc2  2012GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds2t01v43\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
