\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico Peso -4: Economist Dornbusch Urges Weaker Peso \b0\par\par\uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 1996\par 00:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The senior Mexican central banker, who presented a paper on the crisis at the AEA convention, generally explained Mexico's problems in 1994 as rooted in efforts to maintain a fixed exchange rate and in external developments, prominently U.S. interest rate hikes that drew investors away. \par \par \uc2  Dornbusch countered at the AEA panel discussion that \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  - which has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the peso in recent months - was being overly aggressive in fighting inflation and should be more concerned about inflation-adjusted or 'real' appreciation of the peso. \par \par \uc2  He suggested that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shouldn't be as concerned about inflation, calling its attempts to curb price gains 'super dogma.' \par \par \uc2  Dornbusch maintained that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is failing to take into account inflation-adjusted appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because authorities are 'stubbornly attached to inflation fighting.' And he suggested political pressures still exist to strengthen the peso every time a presidential election year rolls around. \par \par \uc2  'The question in Mexico is why is growth in Mexico not at 6%?,' Dornbusch said, compared to official forecasts of up to 3% growth this year. And he maintained that authorities shouldn't be seeking to lower Mexico's inflation rate, which ran at 50% last year, to U.S. norms, which are around 3% or less. Rather, Dornbusch said Mexico should look more for levels around 6% to 7% annual inflation. \par \par \uc2  Gil rebuked Dornbusch, saying that there is 'no substance in the comments.' And the central banker added during the panel discussion, 'I certainly hope, Rudy, you always find central bankers obsessed with inflation. I would really worry if they were not.' \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 07-01-96 \par \par \uc2  2335GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds1700313\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
