\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso -2: One_Year Cetes Back On Auction Block \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Januar 1996\par 21:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Although drops in interest rates often hurt a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , others pointed out that the trend might also be spawning optimism in the prospects of an economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  'What's perhaps very important is the idea that the government is offering one-year Cetes, which gives confidence for long-term prospects,' said Felix Boni, director of equities research with James Capel in Mexico City. \par \par \uc2  As reported, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is offering 364-day Cetes at primary auction Tuesday. It last offered fresh one-year paper Oct. 9, when it was forced to abandon the offer due to insufficient demand. \par \par \uc2  Most economists calculate the Mexican economy contracted a little more than 7% in 1995, but they're predicting that GDP will rally a little more than 2% in 1996 as inflation pressures also ease somewhat. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market took in stride Cabinet changes announced late Friday. As reported, Jesus Reyes Heroles was named to replace Ignacio Pichardo at the Energy Ministry, while Arsenio Farell Cubillas replaced Norma Samaniego at the Federal Auditor's Office. \par \par \uc2  The peso needed some \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support amid light end-of-year selling pressures Friday. While the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not immediately disclose the amount of Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders speculated the amount involved was between $30 million and $50 million. The spot dollar was flirting with the 7.75 marker in light volume when the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  occurred. \par \par \uc2  'People were a little wary of carrying positions at the end of December, but today was very different,' said a local trader. \par \par \uc2  The peso slumped 2.2% in the month of December. It lost 30% against the dollar in nominal terms during 1995, and finished the year down 55% against the dollar since Dec. 20, 1994, when Mexico's financial crisis erupted. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 02-01-96 \par \par \uc2  2017GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds12005ki\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
