\par\par \b \uc2  Mexico's Peso -4: No Immediate Reax To Cabinet Changes \b0\par\par\uc2 182 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Januar 1996\par 16:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  There appeared to be no strong reaction to Cabinet changes announced late Friday. As reported, Jesus Reyes Heroles was named to replace Ignacio Pichardo at the Energy Ministry, while Arsenio Farell Cubillas replaced Norma Samaniego at the Federal Auditor's Office. \par \par \uc2  The peso closed 0.1% weaker against the dollar Friday, despite some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lend support to the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not immediately disclose the amount of Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but traders speculated the amount involved was between $30 million and $50 million. The spot dollar was flirting with the 7.75 marker in light volume when the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  occurred. \par \par \uc2  The peso lost 1.6% against the dollar in the final week of 1995, and slumped 2.2% in the month of December. It lost 30% against the dollar in nominal terms during 1995, and finished the year down 55% against the dollar since Dec. 20, 1994, when Mexico's financial crisis erupted. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 02-01-96 \par \par \uc2  1540GMT \par \par \uc2  1027 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds12004d0\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \par